[h1]Military Drop - Radio Supply Airdrops[/h1]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/guide/images/header.png[/img]

[b]Build 42.21 · Singleplayer & Multiplayer · Standalone[/b]

Tune a military radio to the right frequency, give this week's code and requisition military supplies. A helicopter drops a crate far away and announces the grid to everyone listening... and the noise draws the dead.

[h2]Find the frequency and the code[/h2]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/guide/images/ingame-codebook-memo.png[/img]

Military and police zombies carry memos with the military frequency, different in every game. The code changes every Monday: a numbers station broadcasts it on shortwave, and a military codebook deciphers it.

[h2]Call from your radio[/h2]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/guide/images/radio-logistics-en.png[/img]

Right-click a military radio, [b]Device Options[/b], [b]Logistics[/b] section: type the code and press [b]Request a supply drop[/b]. Walkie-talkie in hand, on the belt or in a bag, or a placed radio.

[h2]Fill the requisition[/h2]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/guide/images/requisition-form-en.png[/img]

Spend a point budget on 18 lots drawn from the game's own loot tables, mods included: rations, medical, ammunition, firearms, fuel... Or order a siren decoy that drags the hordes to a sector you choose.

[h2]Reach the crate[/h2]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/guide/images/ingame-crate-trunk.png[/img]

Hear the helicopter, see its shadow, then race to the announced grid, 150 to 400 tiles away. Everyone on the frequency gets the map marker, and a horde guards the crate. Empty crates can be dismantled for wood.

[h2]Earn the base's trust[/h2]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/guide/images/ingame-console-missions.png[/img]

Recover your drops, send daily reports, announce fallen soldiers' dog tags and answer public missions: recon, horde clearance, radio checks. Trust shortens the wait and unlocks bigger requisitions.

[h2]Hold a liaison post[/h2]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/BATMAN_EHE_MILITARY_DROP/main/docs/guide/images/console-en.png[/img]

Turn a fixed military ham radio into your station's console: transmission log, orders, dog tags, standing and drop requests. In multiplayer, each faction is a station with its own call sign.

[h2]For server admins[/h2]

[list]
[*]44 sandbox options: wait between drops (one week by default, for the whole server), distance, horde, code mode, trust, missions, requisition, decoy.
[*]Requisition lots can be edited, disabled or added in Zomboid/Lua/MilitaryDrop/requisition.txt.
[*]Server-authoritative multiplayer. Admins can force a drop and launch missions from a military radio.
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]

[list]
[*]No other mod required.
[*]Designed to coexist with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3672792485]HEF - Helicopter Event Framework[/url].
[*]With [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3811010882]Signal Smoke[/url], green smoke marks the crate.
[*]Items from your weapon and item mods appear in the crates.
[/list]

